<title>NORWAY: Nycomed Q1 pre-tax falls 33 pct.</title>
<headline>Nycomed Q1 pre-tax falls 33 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months top March 31.</p>
<p>				  (millions of crowns unless states)</p>
<p> Operating revenues		  1,844    vs     1,987</p>
<p> Operating profit before R&amp;D	 493    vs	 648</p>
<p> Research &amp; development costs	189    vs	 206</p>
<p> Operating profit			304    vs	 442</p>
<p> Net financial items	   minus  33    vs  minus 40</p>
<p> Net interest expenses		  40    vs	  35</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			  271    vs	 402</p>
<p> After-tax profit			179    vs	 265</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)     1.75     vs	2.62</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norwegian pharmaceuticals company is Nycomed ASA. A Reuter poll of eight analysts forecast an operating result of 310 million crowns and profits before tax of 280 million crowns. Seven of the analysts recommended to hold the share, while one said sell.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
